<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: ADVISORY-NEW CZECH, SLOVAK PHONE CODES TAKE EFFECT.</title>
<headline>ADVISORY-NEW CZECH, SLOVAK PHONE CODES TAKE EFFECT.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The international country code for dialing the Czech Republic has been changed to +420, and Slovakia's code to +421.</p>
<p>The change, decided by the International Telecommunications Union, reflects the split of former Czechoslovakia in 1993.</p>
<p>The split in codes is expected to help in payment settlement for incoming international calls. The former code common for both countries, +42, has been disconnected. -- Prague Newsroom, +42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
